     "body": "Full run of `go test -timeout 45m ./...` at origin/main 1a3b92688 plus three GUI/webview commits (#2757, #2755, #2753; they change only internal/gui and add internal/webview2env), macOS, sandbox HOME, load average 475–548 from other sessions' suites. These three packages ran past 45m. None of them has an issue for it yet:\n\n- internal/davsync, 2801s. When the timer fired, `TestRestore (1s)` was running, so the package was slow but not hung.\n- internal/provider, 2853s. `TestAgentMCPFiles (45m0s)` was running, with subtest `grok_.grok/config.toml (31s)`. The parent ran for the whole budget: its subtests together take longer than 45m at this load.\n- internal/plugin, 2827s. `TestPiPackage (13m25s)` was running. Before the timeout, TestGatewayHookMixedPiPackage (#2865) and TestHostOnBunLackingLibsSaysWhich (`bunmusl_test.go:237: Providers on a bun lacking libstdc++: starting plugins: context deadline exceeded`) failed, both with #2865's cause.\n\nThe same run also had agent (#2544/#2723), gateway (#2108/#2191, with TestClaudeAccountsSpentFallBackToCodex #2858) and library (#2853) time out, and internal/gui's TestSetAnswersWhileDevinAndProvidersHang (#1375) fail.\n\nNext step: time each of these packages alone at this load, and find out whether TestAgentMCPFiles's per-agent subtests can share the setup they each build.\n",
